# This file exists because the list used to live only in a prompt. A marker dropped from a prompt is
# a fix that silently never shipped, and the whole point of the boundary check is that compiling is
# not shipping.
#
# A MARKER MUST BE A STRING LITERAL, NOT A FUNCTION NAME. `strings` reads the binary's data, so a
# Rust fn name is not there to find. MEASURED: `failed_task_finding` appears 0 times as a literal in
# swarm.rs and would have reported ABSENT after a perfectly correct rebuild, refusing the boundary
# and sending me to fix a defect that did not exist. Verify a candidate first:
#     grep -c '"MARKER"' crates/goose-cli/src/commands/swarm.rs
# and for a marker inside a format! string, remember the fragment SPLITS at each {interpolation} —
# pick text that lies wholly between two of them.

